+/* Create a sealed closure. It is called like any closure, and its function reads the data with
+   zcallee_closure_data(), but nothing else can get to the data through the closure:
+   zclosure_get_data and zclosure_set_data panic on it, and zclosure_new and zclosure_new_sealed
+   refuse to rebind it to other data. The seal is set at creation and cannot be removed.
+
+   This lets a module hand out a callable interface without handing out the state behind it. The
+   seal protects only the path through the closure: the data stays reachable through any other
+   pointer to it, so keep the data private to the module. And if other code can reach `function`
+   itself, it can make its own closure of it with data of its choosing, so keep the function
+   static, or otherwise unexposed, when it must trust its data. */
+void* zclosure_new_sealed(void* function, void* data);
+
+/* Get the data for the given closure. If the passed-in pointer is not a closure pointer, or is a
+   sealed closure, then this panics. */
